<title>PORTUGAL: Refined copper prodn from scrap down yr/yr Jan-Nov.</title>
<headline>Refined copper prodn from scrap down yr/yr Jan-Nov.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Copper refined from copper and copper alloy scrap was lower between January and November 1996 than in the previous period, the International Copper Study Group (ICSG) said.</p>
<p>According to the ICSG, copper refined from copper and copper alloy scrap averaged 14.3 percent of total refined production in the first 11 months of last year, down from 18.7 percent in the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>The lower return is presumed to be largely the market response to lower prices, the ICSG said in a statement.</p>
<p>Mine and refined production of copper were up in the 11 month period by 6.1 and 4.3 percent, respectively, compared with 1995, it said.</p>
<p>The market continued to be nearly in balance with consumption marginally higher than the rate of production for November.</p>
<p>The average LME spot price for November 1996 was $2,230 per tonne, but in December averaged $2,267 per tonne, responding to the tighter market.</p>
